>
  <p>GTA 6 launches <a href="/gta-6/release-date/">November 19, 2026</a>, and robbery is at the heart of it. But a lot of what you'll read online about GTA 6 heists is guesswork. Here's what Rockstar has actually shown, kept separate from the speculation.</p>

  <h2>Confirmed by Rockstar</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The story is about a score.</strong> Rockstar's official description says it begins "when an easy score goes wrong" for Lucia and Jason.</li>
    <li><strong>Raul Bautista is a bank robber who recruits crews.</strong> His official character bio calls him a seasoned bank robber who brings in talent for high-risk, high-reward scores.</li>
    <li><strong>Robbery is in the trailers.</strong> The first trailer (December 2023) shows Lucia and Jason holding up a convenience store.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Confirmed in game: open-world robberies</h2>
  <p>You can rob stores in the open world. From Chapter 2 the map's Robberies menu lists 16 Smash 'n' Grab targets, jewelry stores and pawn shops, each with a security level and take value. See <a href="/gta-6/smash-and-grab/">every smash and grab location</a>, and compare earnings in the <a href="/gta-6/make-money/">money per hour calculator</a>.</p>

  <h2>Confirmed in game: bank robberies</h2>
  <p>Banks are in the same Robberies map menu, split into <strong>Bank Jobs</strong> and <strong>Big Bank Jobs</strong>, with Fleeca, Lombank, ShoreFront and Gibson Brothers branches around Leonida. Each bank's map card shows its security level, a take value, and boxes for the <strong>cash drawer</strong>, <strong>safe</strong> and <strong>vault</strong>. We've robbed two on stream (2026-11-23, Chapter 3):</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>ShoreFront – Ocean Beach.</strong> The teller drawers hold marked bills ($360 a drawer for us). The back-office safe needs a code, or you can blow it, and it paid +$900 and +$3,780. We left with about $13,300 in marked bills in the bag plus about $600 cash, got 3 stars, and lost them with a Clean Getaway while Lucia drove. Her partner menu also offered Distract law.</li>
    <li><strong>Lombank – Ocean Beach.</strong> The card reads "Large bank with marked bills on site. A viable robbery target now that you have a dye pack jammer": medium security, take value $75,000–135,000. We grabbed marked bills from the counters (Lucia's bag hit $6,480) and got out with 3 stars.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="sg-pics" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:10px;max-width:720px">
